  "modified": "2026-10-05T10:59:39Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: a resolver using dns64 with break-dnssec yes could abort when a partially excluded AAAA RRset had been cached with a NOQNAME proof (use-after-free on the filter64 path)\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-19666.patch: clear the NOQNAME proof alias on the DNS64 filter64 path (upstream c185a0d8c5)\n     - CVE-2026-19666\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: a resolver could abort on a wildcard answer whose NOQNAME proof owner carries both a signed NSEC3 and an unsigned NSEC, because the proof was selected by wire position when caching and when serving\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-80274.patch: record the denial type the validator accepted and use it when caching and serving the NOQNAME proof (upstream 2db650ce4e); adds dns_rdataset_addnoqnametype() rather than changing the dns_rdataset_addnoqname() ABI\n     - debian/libdns1104.symbols: record dns_rdataset_addnoqnametype(), added so\n       dns_rdataset_addnoqname() keeps its signature\n     - CVE-2026-80274",
